> linux-pm instead would save some pain there.

I am a bit reluctant about LKML from some of the discussions I have seen=20
there and participated in during CFS / CK discussion. I really didn't=20
like the tone. Its one thing to say ones own oppinion, another one to=20
bash at each other as if there was no tomorrow.

This has been refreshingly different on tuxonice mailing lists. I am also=20
a bit reluctant about the traffic. I already have some quite high traffic=20
mailinglists with 30000-40000 mails a year, but LKML would top these=20
easily I guess and I am not that sure I want to put that load on my mail=20
infrastructure to follow TuxOnIce developments. I think this is a generic=20
problem for testers of specific kernel subsystems...

But then LKML is were TuxOnIce is visible to the kernel developer=20
community.

I would appreciate linux-pm I think maybe with a guideline to CC to LKML=20
in usual cases...

BTW: toi-3.0-rc3 is rocking along nicely on my two ThinkPads (T42 and=20
T23)... I am using 2.6.23.12 with cfs-v24.1...

